* Date: March 04, 2025, 17:31:36
* Template: BEER_reference_3x_GPU.instr.template
*
* %Description
* ToF diffractometer BEER@ESS, primary part (source to sample). Employs the ESS_butterfly.comp source (version 2016)
* and permits easy, quasi-automatic setup for pre-selected operation modes. Provides basic beam characteristics on the output.
* The operation modes are:
* 0	F0	Maximum white beam, never used in experiment
* 1	F1	Accident full beam, F0 with FC choppers running
* 2	F2	Maximum reduced experimental beam, F1, with diffraction slit on
* 3	PS0	Maximum intensity,  pulse shaping, diffraction, max. slit
* 4	PS1	High flux, pulse shaping, in-situ thermo mechanical experiment
* 5	PS2	Medium resolution, pulse shaping, in-situ thermo mechanical experiment
* 6	PS3	High resolution, pulse shaping, in-situ thermo mechanical experiment
* 7	M0	Maximum intensity,  modulation, diffraction, max. slit
* 8	M1	High flux, modulation, strain scanning
* 9	M2	Medium resolution, modulation, strain scanning
* 10	M3	High resolution, modulation, strain scanning
* 11	IM0	White beam, imaging
* 12	IM1	High flux, pulse shaping, imaging, Bragg edge
* 13	SANS	White beam, SANS
* 14	DS0	diffraction + SANS, modulation, in-situ thermomechanical experiment
* 15	DS1	diffraction + SANS, pulse shaping, in-situ thermomechanical experiment
* 16	M4	High resolution, modulation x 4, strain scanning

*
* This instrument model depends on the component Guide_multichannel.comp (J. Saroun, 2016) describing 
* a multichannel neutron guide with semi-transparent blades. It allows to simulate the bi-spectral extraction optics.
* This component is a part of McStas distribution as of ver. 2.5.
* 
* Example: mcrun BEER_reference.instr <parameters=values>
*
* %Parameters
* mode: [] Operation mode (0..15) as defined in the description
* lambda: [AA] Nominal wavelength used to calculate chopper phase
* verbose: [] Set to 1 for a printed report on guides and choppers parameters
* npulse: [] Pulse number to focus at. 
* misfit_h: [m] Random misfit of guide elements, horizontal 
* misfit_v: [m] Random misfit of guide elements, vertical
* monoutputs: [] Set to 0 to skip showing monitor data except of BM1, BM2 and BM3
* %Link
*
* %End
*******************************************************************************/

DEFINE INSTRUMENT BEER_reference(int mode=0, lambda=0, int verbose=0, int npulse=0, misfit_h=2e-5, misfit_v=1e-4, int monoutputs=1)

